
# Docker Image Review Checklist

## Purpose

This checklist is used by the AI Product Manager to review the baseline (fat) and optimized (slim) Docker images before deployment.

The review focuses on configuration, functionality, reproducibility, security, and supporting evidence.

## 1. Docker Image Configuration

- [ ] The fat image uses `python:3.13`.
- [ ] The slim image uses `python:3.13-slim`.
- [ ] The slim image uses a multi-stage build.
- [ ] Both images have the required tags:
  - `ml-infer-fat:1.0`
  - `ml-infer-slim:1.0`
- [ ] Both Dockerfiles are available for review.
- [ ] Dependencies are documented.

## 2. Model and Inference Consistency

- [ ] Both images use the same `model/model.pt`.
- [ ] Both images use the same `app/inference.py`.
- [ ] Input image preprocessing is identical.
- [ ] Both images return top-3 predictions.
- [ ] Predicted classes match in the same order.
- [ ] Confidence score differences are within 0.001.

## 3. Build and Runtime Validation

- [ ] Both Docker images build successfully.
- [ ] Both containers start without errors.
- [ ] Both containers process a valid test image.
- [ ] Runtime logs are available.
- [ ] Build and run commands are documented.

## 4. Optimization Review

- [ ] Image sizes are measured in MB.
- [ ] Build times are recorded.
- [ ] Inference execution times are measured.
- [ ] The slim image is smaller than the fat image.
- [ ] Optimization does not change prediction results.

## 5. Security and Reliability

- [ ] No passwords, tokens, or secrets are stored in the images.
- [ ] Dependencies are reviewed for known vulnerabilities.
- [ ] Unnecessary files are excluded from the images.
- [ ] Runtime errors are handled appropriately.
- [ ] The containers do not require unnecessary privileges.

## 6. Documentation and Evidence

- [ ] Dockerfiles and dependency files are available.
- [ ] Build and run instructions are provided.
- [ ] Inference test results are documented.
- [ ] Optimization measurements are recorded.
- [ ] Known limitations and issues are documented.

